/Title (The Log-Log model is used when both the dependent and independent variables are expected to have a non-linear and elastic relationship. This model assumes that percentage changes in both the dependent and independent variables are related in a constant proportion. It's commonly used when both variables exhibit exponential growth or are affected by similar underlying processes. In this model, the coefficients represent the elasticity between the dependent and independent variables. )
