/Title (The Lin-Log model is appropriate when the relationship between the independent variables and the dependent variable is expected to have diminishing marginal returns, particularly when the independent variables, like population or sectoral contributions, grow rapidly. This model is helpful when the effect of changes in the independent variable diminishes as that independent variable increases. )
